The contents of banks/, states/, results/, summaries/, and exemplars/ are
derivative annotations and evaluation records built on the UT Campus Object
Dataset (CODa), which is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).

These directories are therefore released under the same license:
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

Attribution: (1) the CODa dataset (Zhang et al., IEEE Transactions on Robotics,
vol. 40, pp. 3322-3340, 2024; https://amrl.cs.utexas.edu/coda/), and (2) the
paper "Free the Language Model From the Vision Encoder: Semantic Serialization
as a Perception Interface for Small Language Models" (Xu and Sankar, submitted
to IEEE Access, 2026). No CODa images are redistributed here.

Added 2026-11-15. The data files under exp_rev1/ and serializer/ are records of the same
kind and are released under the same license. The folders exp_rev1/c1_nusc/ and
exp_rev1/c2_nusc/ are built on nuScenes (Caesar et al., CVPR 2020; https://www.nuscenes.org),
which is licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 as well; no nuScenes images are redistributed here.
The paper was revised under the title "Semantic Serialization as a Perception Interface for
Small Language Models in Closed-Set, Task-Aware Embodied Question Answering".
